For any positive integer $h$, the weights $$\gamma_j=\frac{\log(j+2)-\log(j+1)}{\log(h+1)}
  \quad(0\le j<h)$$ are positive, sum to one, and satisfy, for every $d\in\{0,1,2,\ldots\}\cup\{\infty\}$, $$\begin{aligned}
  \phi_h(d)
    &=\sum_{j=0}^{h-1}\gamma_j\mathbf1_{\{d\le j\}},
    \label{eq:profile-expansion}\\
  \sum_{j=0}^{h-1}\gamma_j\mathbf1_{\{d\le3j+2\}}
    &\le\phi_h(d)+\frac{\log3}{\log(h+1)}.
    \label{eq:profile-dilation}
\end{aligned}$$

Let $(N,d,o)$ be a countable pointed metric space such that $d(x,y)\ge1$ for distinct points and $\operatorname{diam}N\le B<\infty$. The map $$J:\ell_1(N\setminus\{o\})\longrightarrow\mathcal F(N),
 \qquad Jc=\sum_{x\ne o}c_x\delta_x,$$ is a linear isomorphism onto $\mathcal F(N)$ and satisfies $$\label{eq:coefficient-bounds}
 \tfrac12\left\|c\right\|_1\le\left\|Jc\right\|\le B\left\|c\right\|_1.$$ If $N\ne\{o\}$, then $\mathcal F(N)$ has $2B$-BAP. If $N=\{o\}$, both spaces are zero.

Suppose that a bounded finite-rank linear operator $T_0:\mathcal F(M_p)\to\mathcal F(M_p)$ satisfies $\left\|T_0\right\|\le p$ and $$\left\|T_0\delta_a-\delta_a\right\|<\frac12\qquad(a\in A_p).$$ Then there are a finite set $S\subseteq M_p$ containing $o$ and a bounded finite-rank linear operator $T:\mathcal F(M_p)\to\mathcal F(M_p)$ such that $$\label{eq:operator-bounds}
 \begin{gathered}
 T\mathcal F(M_p)\subseteq\operatorname{span}\{\delta_j:j\in S\},\qquad
 \left\|T\right\|\le2p,\\
 \left\|T\delta_a-\delta_a\right\|<1\qquad(a\in A_p).
 \end{gathered}$$

Let $S\subseteq M_p$ be finite and contain $o$, and let $T:\mathcal F(M_p)\to\mathcal F(M_p)$ be a bounded linear operator satisfying <a href="#eq:operator-bounds" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:operator-bounds">[eq:operator-bounds]</a>. There is a family $(\mu_x)_{x\in M_p}$ of signed measures on $S$, each of total mass one, such that $$\label{eq:affine-pairing}
 \int g\,d\mu_x=(T\delta_x)(g-g(o))+g(o)$$ for every real Lipschitz function $g$ on $M_p$. They satisfy $$\label{eq:tv-bound}
 \left\|\mu_x\right\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\le V=1+4pB\qquad(x\in M_p),$$ and, for every source vertex $x$, $$\label{eq:bump-mass}
 \int b_x\,d\mu_x\ge\frac{3L}{4}.$$

For a fixed integer $n\ge1$, let $\beta_m$ be the fraction of vertices of $G_m$ from which a matched walk of length $n$ starts. Then $$\label{eq:bad-fraction}
 \limsup_{m\to\infty}\beta_m
 \le |S|\frac Hk\left(\frac{\Delta QH}{k}\right)^n.$$ Consequently one can choose $n\ge2$ and then $m$ so that $\beta_m<1/(20V)$.
